---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Research"
  description="Exbound's public research program: reconstruction methods, technical dossiers, verification, and the legal basis."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Public research program</p>
      <h1>Evidence first</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Reconstruction is driven by reproducible observation of what the
        original software does — not by guesswork. The research repository holds
        the methods, the per-target dossiers, and the verification standards.
      </p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://github.com/exbound/research"
          >Open the research repository</a
        >
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>What's in the research repository</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <a href="https://github.com/exbound/research/blob/main/dossiers/README.md"
              >Target inventory</a
            > — the twelve targets, with objective and initial approach.
          </li>
          <li>
            <a href="https://github.com/exbound/research/blob/main/docs/capability-model.md"
              >Capability model (C1–C9)</a
            > — how reconstruction is measured, and the observed / implemented /
            verified coverage triplet.
          </li>
          <li>
            <a href="https://github.com/exbound/research/blob/main/dossiers/origin.md"
              >Origin dossier</a
            > — the worked example and pilot.
          </li>
          <li>
            <a href="https://github.com/exbound/research/blob/main/docs/legal-basis.md"
              >Legal basis</a
            > — why compatible reconstruction on lawfully held copies is
            defensible, and where the limits are.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Evidence standards</h2>
        <p>
          Every claim carries the command, file, or source that produced it.
          Statements are marked <strong>ESTABLISHED</strong> or
          <strong>HYPOTHESIS / NEEDS-OBSERVATION</strong>, and never promoted
          from one to the other without evidence. Negative results are welcome
          and held to the same standard.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
